.TH MEGACOIN-CLI "1" "October 2026" "megacoin-cli v1.10.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
megacoin-cli \- manual page for megacoin-cli v1.10.0
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B megacoin-cli
[\fI\,options\/\fR] \fI\,<command> \/\fR[\fI\,params\/\fR]  \fI\,Send command to Megacoin Core\/\fR
.br
.B megacoin-cli
[\fI\,options\/\fR] \fI\,-named <command> \/\fR[\fI\,name=value\/\fR]...  \fI\,Send command to Megacoin Core (with named arguments)\/\fR
.br
.B megacoin-cli
[\fI\,options\/\fR] \fI\,help                List commands\/\fR
.br
.B megacoin-cli
[\fI\,options\/\fR] \fI\,help <command>      Get help for a command\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Megacoin Core RPC client version v1.10.0
.SH OPTIONS
.HP
\-?
.IP
This help message
.HP
\fB\-conf=\fR<file>
.IP
Specify configuration file. Relative paths will be prefixed by datadir
location. (default: megacoin.conf)
.HP
\fB\-datadir=\fR<dir>
.IP
Specify data directory
.HP
\fB\-getinfo\fR
.IP
Get general information from the remote server.
.HP
\fB\-named\fR
.IP
Pass named instead of positional arguments (default: false)
.HP
\fB\-rpcclienttimeout=\fR<n>
.IP
Timeout in seconds during HTTP requests, or 0 for no timeout. (default:
900)
.HP
\fB\-rpcconnect=\fR<ip>
.IP
Send commands to node running on <ip> (default: 127.0.0.1)
.HP
\fB\-rpccookiefile=\fR<loc>
.IP
Location of the auth cookie. Relative paths will be prefixed by a
net\-specific datadir location. (default: data dir)
.HP
\fB\-rpcpassword=\fR<pw>
.IP
Password for JSON\-RPC connections
.HP
\fB\-rpcport=\fR<port>
.IP
Connect to JSON\-RPC on <port> (default: 9469 or testnet: 19469)
.HP
\fB\-rpcuser=\fR<user>
.IP
Username for JSON\-RPC connections
.HP
\fB\-rpcwait\fR
.IP
Wait for RPC server to start
.HP
\fB\-rpcwallet=\fR<walletname>
.IP
Send RPC for non\-default wallet on RPC server (needs to exactly match
corresponding \fB\-wallet\fR option passed to megacoind)
.HP
\fB\-stdin\fR
.IP
Read extra arguments from standard input, one per line until EOF/Ctrl\-D.
.HP
\fB\-stdinrpcpass\fR
.IP
Read RPC password from standard input as a single line.
.HP
\fB\-version\fR
.IP
Print version and exit
.PP
Chain selection options:
.HP
\fB\-testnet\fR
.IP
Use the test chain
